use std
into video.amni

Namespace video; imports os. A CPU-only H.264 video encoder and MP4 writer for exporting rendered animations: frames go in as RGBA8 pictures and come out as one .mp4 file that phones, browsers and players open. The stream is H.264 Constrained Baseline (profile 66 with constraint flags 0 and 1, CAVLC entropy coding, 8-bit 4:2:0), one slice per frame, every frame a reference frame, picture order type 2 (output order equals coding order), deblocking switched off in every slice header. Macroblocks are intra 16 by 16 (I frames and anywhere a P frame chooses it), P 16 by 16 with whole-pixel motion vectors, or P skip. Because deblocking is off and every motion vector is a multiple of 4 quarter pixels, the encoder's own reconstruction is exactly what a conforming decoder produces; `recon` exposes it for tests. Every value is a 64-bit `int`; arithmetic shifts round toward minus infinity; clip255(v) limits v to 0 to 255. Nothing here may crash or read outside a list on bad input: problems make the call give false with a reason for `error()`.

```he
