let ZZ int[16] = [0, 1, 4, 8, 5, 2, 3, 6, 9, 12, 13, 10, 7, 11, 14, 15];
let MF int[18] = [13107, 5243, 8066, 11916, 4660, 7490, 10082, 4194, 6554, 9362, 3647, 5825, 8192, 3355, 5243, 7282, 2893, 4559];
let DQ int[18] = [10, 16, 13, 11, 18, 14, 13, 20, 16, 14, 23, 18, 16, 25, 20, 18, 29, 23];
let CQP int[22] = [29, 30, 31, 32, 32, 33, 34, 34, 35, 35, 36, 36, 37, 37, 37, 38, 38, 38, 39, 39, 39, 39];
let LEVELS int[42] = [10, 1485, 99, 11, 3000, 396, 12, 6000, 396, 13, 11880, 396, 21, 19800, 792, 22, 20250, 1620, 30, 40500, 1620, 31, 108000, 3600, 32, 216000, 5120, 40, 245760, 8192, 42, 522240, 8704, 50, 589824, 22080, 51, 983040, 36864, 52, 2073600, 36864];
```

Tables: `CBPINTER` gives the Exp-Golomb code number of a P macroblock's coded block pattern (luma bits 0 to 3 plus 16 times the chroma value). `CTLEN` and `CTBITS` are the coeff_token codes: 4 tables of 68 (table t starts at 68 t; table 0 for nC 0 to 1, 1 for 2 to 3, 2 for 4 to 7, 3 for 8 or more), entry trailing ones plus 4 times total coefficients; `CDCLEN` and `CDCBITS` the same for chroma DC (nC minus 1). `TZLEN` and `TZBITS` are total_zeros codes at (total coefficients minus 1) times 16 plus total zeros; `CTZLEN` and `CTZBITS` the chroma DC ones at (total minus 1) times 4 plus zeros. `RUNLEN` and `RUNBITS` are run_before codes at (zeros left capped at 7, minus 1) times 16 plus the run. `ZZ` is the 4 by 4 zigzag scan: scan position to raster index x plus 4 y. `MF` holds the forward quantizer multipliers and `DQ` the dequantizer scales, 3 per qp modulo 6: the first for positions where x and y are both even, the second where both are odd, the third otherwise. `CQP` is the chroma qp for luma qp 30 to 51 (below 30 they are equal). `LEVELS` lists H.264 levels as triples: level number, largest macroblocks per second, largest macroblocks per frame.

Errors: a module text `why`; `fail(reason)` stores it and gives false; `error()` gives it.

Bit writer: module byte list `bs`, int `acc` and int `nacc` (bits held, below 8). `put(v, n)` appends the low n bits of v (n from 0 to 32), highest first. `ue(v)` writes the unsigned Exp-Golomb code of v: with m the number of bits of v plus 1, m minus 1 zero bits then v plus 1 in m bits. `se(v)` writes `ue` of 2 v minus 1 for positive v and of minus 2 v otherwise. `trailing()` writes a 1 bit then zero bits to the next byte boundary. `nal(type, out)` appends to the byte list out a NAL unit made from bs: the header byte 0x60 plus type, then the bytes of bs with an extra 0x03 inserted wherever two zero bytes in a row would otherwise be followed by a byte of 3 or less; then empties bs.

Session state (module): `width`, `height` (the picture, both even), `cw` and `ch` (rounded up to multiples of 16), `mbw` and `mbh` (macroblocks across and down), `fps`, `qp`, `gop`, frame count `frames`, `frame_num`, IDR count; `sps` and `pps` byte lists (complete NAL units); `samples` (every coded frame's NAL unit, one after another) with int lists `sizes` and `keys` (whether each frame is an IDR); planes `cy`, `cu`, `cv` (the current source, coded size, chroma planes cw/2 by ch/2), `ry`, `ru`, `rv` (the reconstruction being built) and `py`, `pu`, `pv` (the previous reconstruction); module bool `keep_recon` (false at load) and byte list `recon`.

`start(w, h, rate, q, g)` resets everything and gives false when w or h is not positive, odd, above 8192, when the macroblock count is above 36864, when rate is not 1 to 240, or when g is below 1. qp is q limited to 10 to 51. The level is the first entry of the level list whose macroblocks per second (macroblocks per frame times rate) and macroblocks per frame both fit, else 52. SPS into bs: profile 66 in 8 bits, 0xc0 in 8 bits, the level in 8 bits, `ue` 0 (sps id), `ue` 12 (frame numbers are 16 bits), `ue` 2 (picture order type), `ue` 1 (one reference frame), a 0 bit, `ue` of mbw minus 1, `ue` of mbh minus 1, a 1 bit (frames only), a 1 bit (direct 8x8 inference), then the cropping flag: when cw or ch differ from the picture a 1 bit then `ue` 0, `ue` of (cw minus width) halved, `ue` 0, `ue` of (ch minus height) halved, else a 0 bit; then a 0 bit (no VUI) and `trailing`; `nal(7)` into sps. PPS: `ue` 0, `ue` 0, 0 bit (CAVLC), 0 bit, `ue` 0 (one slice group), `ue` 0, `ue` 0, 0 bit, 2 zero bits, `se` 0, `se` 0, `se` 0 (chroma qp offset), a 1 bit (deblocking control present), 0 bit, 0 bit, `trailing`; `nal(8)` into pps.

Color conversion of one RGBA frame into cy, cu, cv (BT.601 limited range): Y is ((66 R plus 129 G plus 25 B plus 128) shifted right by 8) plus 16; for each 2 by 2 block, with R, G, B the rounded averages of its 4 pixels (sum plus 2, shifted right by 2), U is ((minus 38 R minus 74 G plus 112 B plus 128) shifted right by 8) plus 128 and V is ((112 R minus 94 G minus 18 B plus 128) shifted right by 8) plus 128. Alpha is ignored. The area beyond the picture (up to the coded size) repeats the last column, then the last row, of each plane.

`add(rgba)` gives false when rgba is shorter than width times height times 4 or `start` did not succeed. It converts the frame; the frame is an IDR when the frame count is a multiple of gop, which also sets frame_num to 0. It encodes the slice into bs, `nal` type 5 (IDR) or 1 into samples, records its size and key flag, appends the cropped reconstruction to recon (Y width by height, then U, then V, each half by half) when keep_recon is set, swaps the reconstruction into the previous planes, counts the frame and sets frame_num to (frame_num plus 1) modulo 65536.

Slice header: `ue` 0 (first macroblock), `ue` 7 for an IDR (all I) or 5 (all P), `ue` 0 (pps id), frame_num in 16 bits, for an IDR `ue` of the IDR count modulo 2 (counting IDRs from 0), for P a 0 bit (no ref count override) and a 0 bit (no list modification); then for an IDR two 0 bits and for P one 0 bit (reference marking); `se` of qp minus 26; `ue` 1 (deblocking off).

Macroblock records for the frame (module int lists, one per macroblock in raster order): kind (0 skip, 1 P 16 by 16, 2 intra), motion vector x and y in quarter pixels, and 16 luma plus 8 chroma (4 Cb then 4 Cr) total-coefficient counts `tc` for the CAVLC neighbor rule. In P frames a run of skipped macroblocks is counted; before each coded macroblock the run is written with `ue` and reset, and after the last macroblock a nonzero run is written. Then `trailing`.

Block layout: luma 4 by 4 block k (0 to 15) is at x equal to 8 times (k shifted right by 2, bitwise-and 1) plus 4 times (k bitwise-and 1) and y equal to 8 times (k shifted right by 3) plus 4 times ((k shifted right by 1) bitwise-and 1) within the macroblock; chroma block k (0 to 3) is at 4 times (k bitwise-and 1), 4 times (k shifted right by 1) in each 8 by 8 chroma macroblock.

Forward transform and quantization of a 4 by 4 residual r (indexed x plus 4 y), for the encoder only: rows then columns each map (a, b, c, d) to (a plus b plus c plus d, 2 a plus b minus c minus 2 d, a minus b minus c plus d, a minus 2 b plus 2 c minus d). With m equal to qp modulo 6, qbits 15 plus qp divided by 6 and f equal to 2 to the qbits divided by 3 for intra or by 6 for inter, each coefficient's level is (its magnitude times the `MF` entry for m and its position class, plus f) shifted right by qbits, with its sign, limited to minus 2047 to 2047. Intra 16 by 16 DC: the 16 block DC values in a 4 by 4 grid (block position x/4 plus 4 times y/4) go through rows then columns of (a plus b plus c plus d, a plus b minus c minus d, a minus b minus c plus d, a minus b plus c minus d), each result arithmetic shifted right by 1, then quantized with the first `MF` entry and (magnitude times multiplier plus 2 f) shifted right by qbits plus 1. Chroma DC: the 4 DC values (block order) become (c0 plus c1 plus c2 plus c3, c0 minus c1 plus c2 minus c3, c0 plus c1 minus c2 minus c3, c0 minus c1 minus c2 plus c3), quantized like the luma DC but with the chroma qp.

Reconstruction, exactly as the standard's decoding process. Dequantization of a level at a position with qp p: level times the `DQ` entry for p modulo 6 and the position class, shifted left by p divided by 6. Intra 16 by 16 DC: the levels go through the same 4-point Hadamard on rows then columns without a shift; with s equal to 16 times the first `DQ` entry for p modulo 6, each value v becomes (v times s) shifted left by (p divided by 6 minus 6) when p is at least 36, else (v times s plus 2 to the (5 minus p divided by 6)) arithmetic shifted right by (6 minus p divided by 6); it replaces coefficient 0 of its block. Chroma DC (chroma qp pc): the Hadamard of the 4 levels as above, then ((v times 16 times the first `DQ` entry for pc modulo 6) shifted left by pc divided by 6) arithmetic shifted right by 5. Inverse 4 by 4 transform: each row (d0, d1, d2, d3) gives e0 d0 plus d2, e1 d0 minus d2, e2 (d1 arithmetic shifted right by 1) minus d3, e3 d1 plus (d3 arithmetic shifted right by 1), then (e0 plus e3, e1 plus e2, e1 minus e2, e0 minus e3); then each column the same; each result r becomes (r plus 32) arithmetic shifted right by 6 and is added to the prediction with clip255.

Intra 16 by 16 prediction from the reconstruction of the current frame (top row available when the macroblock row is above 0, left column when the column is above 0): mode 0 vertical copies the row above; 1 horizontal copies each row's left pixel; 2 DC is (sum of the 16 above plus the 16 left plus 16) shifted right by 5, or with only one side (its sum plus 8) shifted right by 4, or 128 with neither; 3 plane, with p(x, y) the reconstructed pixels around (p(-1, -1) the above-left one): H is the sum over i from 0 to 7 of (i plus 1) times (p(8 plus i, -1) minus p(6 minus i, -1)), V the same down the left column, a is 16 times (p(-1, 15) plus p(15, -1)), b (5 H plus 32) arithmetic shifted right by 6, c (5 V plus 32) arithmetic shifted right by 6 and each pixel clip255((a plus b times (x minus 7) plus c times (y minus 7) plus 16) arithmetic shifted right by 5). Vertical needs the top, horizontal the left, plane both. The encoder tries every allowed mode and keeps the one with the smallest sum of absolute differences from the source.

Chroma intra prediction for each 8 by 8 plane with the same availability: mode 0 DC per 4 by 4 block, using sums of that block's own 4 pixels above and 4 to its left: blocks 0 and 3 use (both sums plus 4) shifted right by 3 when both sides exist, else the side that exists (sum plus 2, shifted right by 2), else 128; block 1 (top right) prefers the top, then the left, then 128; block 2 (bottom left) prefers the left, then the top, then 128. Mode 1 horizontal, 2 vertical, 3 plane: H is the sum over i from 0 to 3 of (i plus 1) times (p(4 plus i, -1) minus p(2 minus i, -1)), V the same on the left, a 16 times (p(-1, 7) plus p(7, -1)), b (34 H plus 32) arithmetic shifted right by 6, c the same with V, each pixel clip255((a plus b times (x minus 3) plus c times (y minus 3) plus 16) arithmetic shifted right by 5). The encoder picks the mode with the smallest summed difference over both planes.

Inter prediction from the previous reconstruction with motion vector (mx, my) in quarter pixels, both multiples of 4: luma pixel (x, y) of the macroblock at (X, Y) copies the previous luma at column X plus x plus mx divided by 4 limited to 0 to cw minus 1 and row likewise limited to 0 to ch minus 1. Chroma uses the same vector in eighth pixels: with xi equal to the chroma macroblock x plus x plus (mx arithmetic shifted right by 3), fx equal to mx bitwise-and 7, and yi, fy likewise, the value is ((8 minus fx)(8 minus fy) A plus fx (8 minus fy) B plus (8 minus fx) fy C plus fx fy D plus 32) shifted right by 6 with A at (xi, yi), B one to the right, C one down, D both, every coordinate limited to the chroma plane.

Motion vector prediction for macroblock (mx0, my0): neighbors A left, B above, C above right (when it is outside the picture use D, above left, instead). A neighbor that exists counts as available; its reference is 0 with its vector for skip and P macroblocks and -1 with vector 0 for intra ones; a missing neighbor has reference -1 and vector 0. When B and C are both missing and A exists, B and C take A's values. Then when exactly one of A, B, C has reference 0 the prediction is its vector, else the median of the three per component. The skip vector is 0 when A or B is missing, or A has reference 0 and vector 0, or B has reference 0 and vector 0; otherwise it is the prediction.

Coding a P frame macroblock: first the skip vector's prediction is formed and its residual transformed and quantized for luma and chroma; when every level is zero the macroblock is skipped (its reconstruction is the prediction). Otherwise a whole-pixel search starts from the best of the skip vector, the prediction and zero, then repeats a small diamond (one pixel left, right, up, down) around the best until no step improves, at most 32 steps and never more than 64 pixels from zero; the cost is the sum of absolute luma differences plus lambda times the bits of the two `se` codes of the vector minus the prediction (in quarter pixels), lambda being 2 to the ((qp minus 12) divided by 6) at least 1. The intra 16 by 16 cost is its best sum of absolute differences plus 6 lambda; the cheaper wins. A P macroblock writes `ue` 0, `se` of the vector difference x then y, `ue` of `CBPINTER` for its coded block pattern, `se` 0 when the pattern is not 0, then the luma blocks of each 8 by 8 quarter whose pattern bit is set (each 16 coefficients, blocks in order k), then chroma. Luma quarter q (blocks 4 q to 4 q plus 3) has bit q set when any of its levels is nonzero; the chroma value is 2 when any chroma AC level is nonzero, else 1 when any chroma DC level is, else 0. Levels outside coded parts count as zero for the reconstruction and their blocks have 0 total coefficients.

Coding an intra 16 by 16 macroblock: its type number is 1 plus the luma mode plus 4 times the chroma value plus 12 when any luma AC level is nonzero; I frames write `ue` of it and P frames `ue` of it plus 5. Then `ue` of the chroma mode, `se` 0 (qp change), the luma DC block (16 levels in zigzag order, nC from block 0's neighbors), then when the type has the 12 the 16 AC blocks (scan positions 1 to 15), then chroma: when the chroma value is not 0 the Cb DC then the Cr DC (4 levels each, nC minus 1), and when it is 2 the 4 Cb AC blocks then the 4 Cr AC blocks (scan positions 1 to 15). The total coefficients kept for luma blocks are those of their AC blocks (0 without the 12), for chroma those of the AC blocks (0 below 2).

nC for a luma block: the left neighbor block (in this macroblock, or the macroblock to the left when it exists) and the top neighbor block likewise; a skipped neighbor macroblock gives 0; with both available (left plus top plus 1) shifted right by 1, with one that one, else 0. Chroma AC blocks use the same rule inside their own plane.

CAVLC block `block(levels, n, nc)` for n coefficients in scan order: the total is the count of nonzero levels; trailing ones are the number of levels of magnitude 1 at the end of the nonzero list (highest scan positions first), at most 3, stopping at the first other one. coeff_token: for nc minus 1 the `CDCLEN` and `CDCBITS` entry trailing plus 4 total, else the table for nc and the same entry. When the total is 0 nothing else follows. The nonzero levels are then written from the highest scan position down: first one sign bit per trailing one (1 for negative); then the rest with a suffix length that starts at 1 when the total is above 10 and trailing ones are below 3, else 0: the level code is 2 times the level minus 2 for positive levels and minus 2 times the level minus 1 for negative ones, less 2 for the first of them when trailing ones are below 3; with suffix length 0 a code below 14 is that many zero bits and a 1, below 30 it is 14 zeros, a 1 and the code minus 14 in 4 bits, otherwise 15 zeros, a 1 and the code minus 30 in 12 bits; with suffix length s above 0 a code below 15 shifted left by s is (code shifted right by s) zeros, a 1 and the low s bits, otherwise 15 zeros, a 1 and the code minus (15 shifted left by s) in 12 bits; after each level the suffix length becomes 1 when it was 0, then grows by 1 when the level's magnitude is above 3 shifted left by (suffix length minus 1) and it is below 6. When the total is below n, total zeros (the zeros before the last nonzero level) follow from `TZLEN`/`TZBITS`, or `CTZLEN`/`CTZBITS` when n is 4; then for each nonzero level from the highest down except the lowest, while zeros are left, the run of zeros just below it from `RUNLEN`/`RUNBITS`, taking it off the zeros left.

MP4 (`finish(out)`): false when no frames were added. Boxes are a 32-bit big-endian size, a 4-letter type and the contents; full boxes add a version byte and 3 flag bytes. ftyp: "isom", 512, then "isom", "iso2", "avc1", "mp41". moov: mvhd version 0 (two zero times, timescale 1000, duration frames times 1000 divided by fps, rate 0x00010000, volume 0x0100, 10 zero bytes, the unity matrix 0x00010000, 0, 0, 0, 0x00010000, 0, 0, 0, 0x40000000, 24 zero bytes, next track 2); trak with tkhd version 0 flags 3 (two zero times, track 1, 4 zero bytes, the same duration, 8 zero bytes, layer, group and volume 0, 2 zero bytes, the matrix, width and height shifted left by 16); mdia with mdhd version 0 (two zero times, timescale fps, duration frames, language 0x55c4, 0), hdlr (4 zero bytes, "vide", 12 zero bytes, "VideoHandler" and a zero byte), minf with vmhd flags 1 (8 zero bytes), dinf holding dref (1 entry: "url " full box flags 1, no contents), and stbl: stsd with 1 entry "avc1" (6 zero bytes, reference index 1 in 16 bits, 16 zero bytes, width and height in 16 bits, 0x00480000 twice, 4 zero bytes, frame count 1 in 16 bits, 32 zero bytes, depth 0x0018 and 0xffff in 16 bits, then an "avcC" box: 1, the SPS's bytes 1, 2 and 3, 0xff, 0xe1, the SPS length in 16 bits and its bytes, 1, the PPS length and bytes); stts (1 entry: frames, 1); stss (the 1-based numbers of the key frames); stsc (1 entry: 1, frames, 1); stsz (size 0, frames, each frame's size plus 4); stco (1 entry: the file offset where the first sample starts). Then mdat holding every sample as its 32-bit big-endian length and its bytes. The moov is built first with offset 0, measured, then built again with the real offset (the ftyp size plus the moov size plus 8). Fails when the file would reach 4 GiB.

`save(path)` runs `finish` and writes the file with `os::write_file`, giving false with a reason when either fails. `frame_bytes(i)` gives frame i's coded size. `psnr_y()` gives the luma PSNR in dB (a real) of the last added frame's reconstruction against its source over the picture area, or 99 when they are equal.
